Z||000003||terryk||10-11-2001||07:21 PM||||I'll bet they're blowing out 3rd gear?<P>If you look at the shift torque management, they really back off the spark on a 2-3 upshift. My trans man is waiting for me to blow out 3rd on my 4T60EHD with so little shift torque limiting.<P>Blowing the TC out the bottom doesn't count!<P>I believe the GM Powertrain site listed the Getrag at 200ft-lbs while the 4T60E and 65E are 280 ft-lbs engine and 400 gear box(racking my brain right now). <P>The ratings are for all gears so, it depends on where you blow them up. The stripped cheese grater I was should happened on a 4T60EHD on a 2-3. Only thing I've seen on Getrags is broken cases and worn syncro's.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 10-11-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000004||terryk||10-11-2001||07:32 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.gm.com/automotive/gmpowertrain/transmissions/4t65_main.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gm.com/automotive/gmpowertrain/transmissions/4t65_main.htm</A> <P>This is the 4T65E (60E is the same rating). I'm looking for the old Getrag page. It's still there but you can't access it through this site.<P>I wonder if the boost control solenoid could be used for the force control motor......Hmmmmmmmmmmmmmm<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 10-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Bob||10-11-2001||08:42 PM||||So is there anything that could be changed in the auto tranny to beef it up? Technically you could control the hp of the motor(from boost) with the boost solenoid, but why would you want to terryk? (I dont follow)||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||10-11-2001||09:35 PM||||A friend and I have some Series II SC's with 4T60E's and Getrag's running on the 94/95 ECM which has a removable mem-cal (chip). I've always thought that I couldn't get the 4T65E to work in that ECM. Now I'm starting to think I can.<P>Main advantage is being able to change the calibrations and get away from the flash PCM's that normally come with the 4T65E/S2 setups. Faking out the PCM is goofy.||||reg||1
